{#
    One name the league cannot read, in one of two shapes.

    **A live question gets buttons.** The whole cost of this screen is the
    number of names on it, and a dropdown is two interactions for what is
    usually one: the suggestion is right about three times in four, so it is one
    tap. They are radio inputs wearing button clothes — there is no JavaScript
    framework here, and each row has to hold an independent answer while one
    submit at the bottom commits the lot.

    **A settled question gets a select.** Nothing came close to it, so it
    arrives answered and the only thing left to do is disagree — and disagreeing
    means finding one blader among forty-eight. `Orteborn` is three edits from
    `Otrebor`, past `AliasResolver::CLOSE_ENOUGH`, so it is offered nothing and
    defaults to a duplicate unless somebody recognises the name. A native picker
    is what that job wants; forty-eight radios in a scroll box is what it does
    not.

    The split also settles a hazard. Everything that can answer a row has to be
    **one control or one radio group**: a `<select>` sharing the field name with
    radios posts alongside them and, being later in the document, quietly wins —
    blanking a button somebody had already pressed. One shape per row and the
    question never arises. It costs a lot of markup too: the whole league
    repeated per row was 700 inputs on the 23 August bracket, and it is now four
    short candidate lists and ten selects.

    At 375px the suggestion is full-width with the other two beneath it, so the
    answer that is usually right is also the biggest target. All three sit in a
    row once there is room.

    A live row carries `required`, so the browser refuses to submit until it is
    answered. A settled row never does — it arrives with an answer, and a
    required control inside a closed disclosure would be one the browser cannot
    focus, blocking the form with nothing on screen to fix.
#}
{% set base = 'flex min-h-11 cursor-pointer items-center justify-center rounded-field border px-3 py-2 text-center text-xs font-black uppercase tracking-wider transition-colors' %}
{% set idle = ' border-line bg-canvas text-ink-muted hover:border-ink-ghost hover:text-ink' %}
{# The suggestion is the primary action, so it reads as one before it is
   pressed rather than only after. It is still unselected: the tint says
   "start here", not "this is decided". #}
{% set proposed = ' border-brand-strong/40 bg-brand-strong/5 text-brand-bright hover:border-brand-strong hover:bg-brand-strong/10' %}
{% set best = decision.isCollision ? null : decision.best %}
{% set others = decision.isCollision ? [] : decision.otherCandidates %}

<li class="space-y-2.5 border-t border-line/40 pt-4 first:border-0 first:pt-0">
    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-baseline gap-x-2">
        <span class="font-mono text-sm font-bold text-ink">{{ decision.name }}</span>
        <span class="text-[11px] text-ink-faint">{{ decision.context }}</span>
    </div>

    {% if decision.isCollision %}
        <twig:Alert tone="heat">
            {{ decision.problem }}
            No alias can settle that &mdash; two rows for one person is a merge, and a blader whose name shadows an alias is the alias to remove.
        </twig:Alert>

    {% elseif decision.hasNothingClose %}
        <label class="sr-only" for="d-{{ decision.key }}">Who {{ decision.name }} is</label>
        <select id="d-{{ decision.key }}" name="decision[{{ decision.key }}]" class="field">
            <option value="create"{{ decision.answer == 'create' ? ' selected' : '' }}>Somebody new</option>
            <option value="drop"{{ decision.answer == 'drop' ? ' selected' : '' }}>Not a person</option>
            <optgroup label="No &mdash; this is">
                {% for id, name in bladers %}
                    <option value="blader:{{ id }}"{{ decision.answer == 'blader:' ~ id ? ' selected' : '' }}>{{ name }}</option>
                {% endfor %}
            </optgroup>
        </select>

    {% else %}
        <fieldset>
            <legend class="sr-only">Who {{ decision.name }} is</legend>

            <div class="grid grid-cols-2 gap-2{{ best ? ' sm:grid-cols-3' : '' }}">
                {% if best %}
                    <div class="col-span-2 sm:col-span-1">
                        <input type="radio" class="peer sr-only" required
                               id="d-{{ decision.key }}-link"
                               name="decision[{{ decision.key }}]"
                               value="blader:{{ best.player.id }}"
                               {{ decision.answer == 'blader:' ~ best.player.id ? 'checked' : '' }}>
                        <label for="d-{{ decision.key }}-link"
                               class="{{ base }}{{ proposed }} peer-checked:border-brand-strong peer-checked:bg-brand-strong/15 peer-checked:text-brand peer-focus-visible:ring-2 peer-focus-visible:ring-brand-strong">
                            <span class="truncate">{{ best.player.name }}</span>
                        </label>
                        <p class="mt-1 text-[10px] italic text-ink-faint">{{ best.because }}</p>
                    </div>
                {% endif %}

                <div>
                    <input type="radio" class="peer sr-only" {{ best ? 'required' : '' }}
                           id="d-{{ decision.key }}-new"
                           name="decision[{{ decision.key }}]"
                           value="create"
                           {{ decision.answer == 'create' ? 'checked' : '' }}>
                    <label for="d-{{ decision.key }}-new"
                           class="{{ base }}{{ idle }} peer-checked:border-positive-strong peer-checked:bg-positive-strong/15 peer-checked:text-positive peer-focus-visible:ring-2 peer-focus-visible:ring-positive-strong">
                        New blader
                    </label>
                </div>

                <div>
                    <input type="radio" class="peer sr-only" {{ best ? 'required' : '' }}
                           id="d-{{ decision.key }}-drop"
                           name="decision[{{ decision.key }}]"
                           value="drop"
                           {{ decision.answer == 'drop' ? 'checked' : '' }}>
                    <label for="d-{{ decision.key }}-drop"
                           class="{{ base }}{{ idle }} peer-checked:border-heat-strong peer-checked:bg-heat-strong/15 peer-checked:text-heat peer-focus-visible:ring-2 peer-focus-visible:ring-heat-strong">
                        Not a person
                    </label>
                </div>
            </div>

            {# The rest of the shortlist, and only ever that — radios, because
               they share the group above, and short because it is candidates
               rather than the league. Opens by itself when the answer is one of
               them, so a re-render never hides the choice that was made. #}
            {% if others is not empty %}
                <details class="mt-2"{{ decision.reachesPastTheShortlist ? ' open' : '' }}>
                    <summary class="inline-flex min-h-11 cursor-pointer list-none items-center text-[11px] font-semibold text-ink-faint transition-colors hover:text-brand sm:min-h-0">
                        {{ others|length }} other {{ others|length == 1 ? 'candidate' : 'candidates' }}&hellip;
                    </summary>

                    <div class="mt-2 space-y-1 rounded-field border border-line/60 bg-canvas p-3">
                        {% for candidate in others %}
                            <label class="flex min-h-11 cursor-pointer items-center gap-2 rounded-control px-2 text-xs hover:bg-surface/60 sm:min-h-9">
                                <input type="radio" name="decision[{{ decision.key }}]" value="blader:{{ candidate.player.id }}"
                                       {{ decision.answer == 'blader:' ~ candidate.player.id ? 'checked' : '' }}>
                                <span class="font-semibold text-ink">{{ candidate.player.name }}</span>
                                <span class="text-[10px] italic text-ink-faint">{{ candidate.because }}</span>
                            </label>
                        {% endfor %}
                    </div>
                </details>
            {% endif %}
        </fieldset>
    {% endif %}
</li>
